Summary: Rebuild the Maven project with updated dependencyManagement and Jackson exclusions

Reasoning:
Okay, so I've been wrestling with dependency conflicts, specifically around Jackson and some core Spring components. My current strategy is to get explicit control over these versions 
right at the root `pom.xml`. I've gone ahead and added explicit version overrides for the Spring Framework components themselves, Tomcat, Micrometer, and crucially, 
`com.fasterxml.jackson.core`.

But just doing that in the root might not be enough if other modules are bringing in their own versions or transitive dependencies. So, to double down, I've also added exclusions for the 
`tools.jackson.core` artifact from the `spring-boot-starter-webmvc` in the `task-web/pom.xml`. This is to ensure that the `com.fasterxml.jackson.core` that I've carefully defined at the 
root is the one that gets picked up and used throughout.

The next logical step, of course, is to rebuild the entire project. This is the moment of truth – I need to see if these targeted overrides and exclusions have actually fixed the 
underlying issues I was facing, and more importantly, if the build still completes successfully. If it builds clean, I'll consider this a significant step in the right direction for 
dependency management.

